---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { company } from '../data/company';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="KCNEX Innovations is a software development studio offering software and app development, web design and development, DevOps, and digital marketing. Built in India, serving the US, UK, and Canada."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">A studio that ships end to end</h1>

      <div class="prose lede">
        <p>
          KCNEX Innovations is a software development studio. We design and
          build software, apps, and websites; we run the DevOps that keeps them
          shipping; and we do the digital marketing that gets them in front of
          customers. Develop, deploy, grow — one team, the whole way.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose body">
        <h2>Where the method comes from</h2>
        <p>
          Before KCNEX took on client work, we built our own product. It
          started with a specific incident: a founder watched a family member
          nearly lose everything to a tech-support scam. A fake pop-up, a phone
          number, and a request to install remote-access software. Every piece
          of technology needed to stop it already existed — it had simply never
          been assembled for the person actually at risk.
        </p>
        <p>
          Building <a href="https://kinsentry.com">KinSentry</a> to close that
          gap meant doing everything ourselves: the product, the
          infrastructure, the release pipeline, and the work of reaching the
          people who needed it. That end-to-end discipline is the method we now
          offer to clients.
        </p>

        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <p>
          Four service lines: software and app development, website and web app
          design and development, DevOps services, and digital marketing. Most
          engagements combine at least two — the product we build is usually
          the product we deploy, and often the product we help grow.
        </p>

        <h2>What we are, honestly</h2>
        <p>
          We are a small team, not an enterprise. We are built in {company.builtIn},
          and we serve clients and users in the {company.serves.join(', ')}. We
          would rather tell you that plainly than dress it up — you can judge
          the work on what it does.
        </p>
        <p>
          KCNEX is the company. <a href="https://kinsentry.com">KinSentry</a> is
          our own shipped product. Client work and future products will each
          stand on their own, and each will be listed on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>How we think about trust</h2>
        <p>
          Clients hand us their codebases, their infrastructure, and sometimes
          their customers' data. We think that trust is earned by being boring
          and verifiable — saying what we will do, documenting what we touch,
          answering when something breaks, and never claiming more than we can
          demonstrate.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you find something on this site that is inaccurate, we want to know.
          Write to <a href={`mailto:${company.email.general}`}>{company.email.general}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 60px);
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 20px);
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .body {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
